### Scenarios covered (all `[S]`, one `@QuarkusTest` boot)
- **A1** badge→PIN→SESSION→200 €→VENTE; `C04-S\d{5}` OPEN in DB *(kept from calibration)*
- **A2** relock with session open → **direct to sale**, no second session (same number)
- **A3** 3 wrong PINs → `COMPTE VERROUILLÉ`; good PIN refused during lockout, accepted after expiry; counters reset
- **A4** badge prefills login (unlock without typing login); one-shot mailbox proven
- **A5** badge while logged in → **ignored** (no operator switch, no line)
- **A6** wrong current / mismatch / success (`Code PIN modifié`) + reconnect on new PIN
- **A7** logout abandons memory cart, draft stays **OPEN & intact** in DB

No `[V]`/`[N]` residue — group A is entirely `[S]`.

### Iterations: 3 runs
1. a1–a4 green; a5/a6/a7 timed out — A4's leftover `/lock` page kept polling and **stole the one-shot badge mailbox**.
2. Added `page.close()` per test → a6 green; a5/a7 still failing.
3. Fixed a5 + a7 → **7/7**.

### Hard points
- **One-shot badge mailbox is shared server state** → must close pages so a lingering `/lock` poll doesn't steal the next test's badge.
- **A5 "ignored" is partly client-invisible**: `UnknownScanHandler` writes the message without `touch()`, so `CODE INCONNU` never reaches the poll — asserted **server-side** via `@Inject PosState` (operator unchanged, empty cart, `transientError` landed on the unknown handler).
- **A2/A4/A7 must cross `/drawer-error`**: unlock opens the drawer; with a session open the redirect hits guarded `/`, so the physical drawer-close carries the poll back to `/` (which itself proves direct-to-sale routing).
- **`#resumeScreen` is `display:none`** until activated → waited on the visible `CAISSE FERMÉE` to confirm logout.
- **A3 lockout expiry** can't wait 5 real minutes → aged `lockedUntil` into the past via `QuarkusTransaction` (only scaffolding outside the HTTP surface).
- **Isolation** via `@TestMethodOrder(MethodName)` + one shared session (A1 opens it on the fresh drop-and-create DB); A6 restores PIN 1234, A3 ends unlocked.

**No `src/main` changes** — only `GroupAIT.java` was touched; nothing committed.

One thing to flag as a design observation (not a bug, so I did **not** modify source per the scope rule): `UnknownScanHandler` setting `transientError` without `touch()` means a `CODE INCONNU` from a bare hardware-bus scan on an idle sale screen won't render until the next touch-producing action — relevant when you get to B7/O-A.

