## Summary

**Group D — Fidélité**, all 3 `[S]` scenarios, one `@QuarkusTest` class, one boot (~21 s): `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` — **BUILD SUCCESS**.

| Id | What it proves |
|----|----|
| **D1** | Card scanned mid-cart (`789…`) → icon `#fidIcon.active`, in-memory `fidelity`, and the card copied onto the **durable draft** (`Ticket.fidelityCard` in H2). |
| **D2** | Manual `/fidelity` fallback attaches the same way; a second entry replaces the first (**last wins**); a follow-up scan syncs the winner onto the draft. |
| **D3** | Card on the lock screen is **inert** — nothing attaches, overlay never flips to PIN (a 15-digit card is not the 8-digit badge), register stays locked. |

**Key mechanics found in `src/main` (read-only):** recognition via `scan.pattern.fidelity=^789\d{12}$`; the scan path funnels through `TicketService.processScan → syncAndRevalue` and persists immediately, while the manual POST path attaches in-memory only — so D2 needs a trailing scan to make persistence observable.

**Iterations:** 2 — first pass green on D1/D2; D3 failed waiting on the hidden `#resumeScreen` overlay, fixed by anchoring on the initially-visible `CAISSE FERMÉE` screen.

**Residue:** the "survives restart" half of D1 is cross-referenced to **K1** (a real `kill -9`/reboot can't run inside one `@QuarkusTest`) — its durable precondition (card on the OPEN draft, which `TicketRecoveryService` reads back on boot) is asserted here. No `[V]`/`[N]` scenarios exist in group D, so there is no skipped-infrastructure residue.

Note: I only touched the new test class `src/test/java/com/intermarche/pos/e2e/GroupDIT.java` and `reports/D.md` — nothing under `src/main`.
