## GroupFIT — done, green

`mvn -q verify -DskipUTs=true -Dit.test=GroupFIT -DskipITs=false` → **Tests run: 7, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** (one Quarkus boot, ~70 s). Only the test class and `reports/F.md` were touched; `src/main` is untouched.

**Scenarios covered ([S]):** F1 (espèces exactes/trop-perçu + rendu + tiroir), F2 (CB partielle + espèces, restant juste à chaque étape), F3 (TPE virtuel accept/refuse/annulation), F4 (bon encodé/Catalina/générique/motif inconnu/plafonnement), F5 (chèque + TR, tiroir ouvert, théorique espèces inchangé), F6 (arrondi solidaire toggle/re-toggle), F8 (numérotation séquentielle, chaîne de signatures SHA-256, grand total perpétuel, ventilation TVA, ticket imprimé).

**Justified residue:** **F7** — tagged `[V]` in the catalog header (`[S] ([V] pour F7)`), so skipped per the "[S]-only" campaign rule; its two-button contract is nonetheless exercised incidentally by F8. Plus the `[V]` valuation sub-clause of F6. No `[N]` in this letter.

**Iterations:** 2. First run: F1/F6/F8 green; three fixes needed —
1. **F5** diverted to `/drawer-error` (cheque opens the drawer, next payment POST is drawer-guarded) → close the drawer between cheque and TR.
2. **F4 Catalina** un-typeable — the payment numpad collapses a leading zero, so a `0482…` number can't be keyed → present encoded/Catalina vouchers on the **scan bus** (the intended `VoucherScanHandler` path during payment).
3. **F2/F3 card accept = 404** — under `@QuarkusTest` the mock `MockHardwareResource` (`@Path("/api/hardware")`) shadows `PosHardwareResource`'s `/api/hardware/tpe/*`, so the inbound TPE endpoints are unreachable.

**Hardest point / notable decision:** the virtual-TPE accept/refuse is the one gesture with **no HTTP surface under test** (shadowed by the hardware simulator). I drive it through the injected `PaymentService.confirmPendingCard`/`refusePendingCard` — the exact call the endpoint wraps — documented as the same justified-scaffolding category as injected-state and DB-aging oracles. Parking, register-cancel and completion all stay on the screen. Full write-up in `reports/F.md`.

Note: I staged nothing and made no commit (you didn't ask me to) — the working tree has the new `GroupFIT.java` and `reports/F.md`.
