## Result

`GroupJIT` — **3 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped**, BUILD SUCCESS (one Quarkus boot, ~30 s). Every group-J scenario is `[S]` and implemented; no `[V]`/`[N]` residue exists in the group.

## Scenarios covered

- **J1 — Entrée/sortie sous avenant.** Endorsed toggle flips `trainingMode`; the orange banner rises on both faces (cashier sale screen `.overlay-training`, customer display `#trainingBanner` via its poll) and both cleanly disappear on exit, leaving an empty cart.
- **J2 — Neutralisation fiscale.** Scans accepted, pay overlay banner shown, cash tender completes in memory — yet **no draft** (`ticketDbId` null, C04 `Ticket` count unchanged), **drawer never opened** (stays `CLOSED`), receipt is a `MODE FORMATION / TICKET NON VALABLE / SANS VALEUR` slip with no register number, and the open session is left pristine.
- **J3 — Actions bloquées.** Reprint refused on button **and** URL (no duplicata printed), refund request refused (no endorsement, no `Refund` created), and every session mutation blocked — `close-start` on the Z button and its GET URL, plus the POST-only `open`/`close` on the request bus — session untouched.

## Iterations

1. J1/J2 green first pass; J3 timed out — the session routes are drawer-guarded (login pulse left the drawer out) and `open`/`close` are `@POST` (a GET `navigate` can't reach them).
2. Added a `closeDrawer()` before the block, kept `close-start` (a real `@GET`) on both button+URL, and probed the POST-only mutations on the request bus. All green.

## Hard points & residue

- **`syncDraft` returning null** is the single training guard — J2 proves neutralization three independent ways.
- **The refund method links aren't a distinct path**: `submitAction` submits the staging form and cancels the href, so a refund only fires via `GET /return/pay/{method}` — exercised on a staged line, matching the GroupH doctrine.
- **Justified residue**: J2's *literal* "login-with-no-session-goes-straight-to-sale" routing can't be bootstrapped through the screen (training's only toggle needs an open session that can't be closed in training); its fiscal essence is proven instead. J3's refund button/URL collapse to one server route.

